From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:45:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 157/207] dsv41 runner trace: drop a name's binding on any
 reassignment

A name the model reassigned stayed bound to its first value, so the
trace form could state a value right for the bound span but wrong for
what the model meant ("Let N=280,223,976,814,164 ... Step3 N=... Compute
N*65536" claimed a value 12,816 off; "N=0 ... N = N*256 + b" claimed
0*256 + 118).

Every `Name =` not after an operator now counts as an assignment,
including a label before the name (`Step3 N=`), `Let N =`, a right side
that does not parse (`N = N*256 + b`), and approximate or hypothetical
text. A bound name is poisoned (the trace abstains) unless the new right
side is the same integer (runner_trace_value.same, cut at a doubt); an
unbindable first sighting blocks later binding; a name states only on
its first bindable definition. Notation the parser refuses (`1|2`,
`1e9+7`) poisons rather than being normalized.

(cherry picked from commit c17578b72c8f77db257f95f8ede3a80468a314a7)
